  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CQL: fix two implementation bugs - and parse rows without the metadata",
  "description": "One is simply copy-pasta, that we did not indicate the correct subtree variable to use.\nThe other is misuse of when/how to add a substree. It doesn't fully fix parsing without metadata, but it makes it slightly better (we do not crash).\n\nSecond patch now fixes parsing without metadata - it was ignoring -1 and -2 lengths, which are NULL and 'not set'. Now parsing works fully.\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaniv Kaul <mykaul@gmail.com>",
